    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Paul Reynolds are delighted to bring to market \"Erin's Cottage\" situated on the highly regarded College Farm Road, Letterkenny.\n\nThis attractive three-bedroom dormer property offers a rare combination of space, privacy and convenience, all within comfortable walking distance of Letterkenny town centre.\nSet on a generous site the property occupies a mature and established setting, surrounded by well-maintained gardens and mature trees. The spacious grounds provide excellent privacy and ample outdoor space.\n\nThe property extends to a well-proportioned two-storey dormer-style residence, with bright and welcoming accommodation throughout. The comfortable sitting room features a traditional fireplace and large picture window overlooking the mature gardens. The kitchen/dining area enjoys excellent natural light and direct access the rear garden & paved patio area, creating a pleasant space for everyday family living and entertaining.\nComprising three bedrooms, one of which is located on the ground floor with a further 2 bedrooms on the first floor, one of which is ensuite. \n\nExternally, the mature gardens are a particular feature, with established planting, lawned areas and a private setting that is increasingly difficult to find so close to town. \n\nCollege Farm Road is a well-established residential location, offering the convenience of town living while retaining the feeling of a spacious countryside setting. Letterkenny's extensive range of shops, schools, healthcare facilities, restaurants, leisure amenities and services are all readily accessible.\n\nThis is an appealing family home with excellent potential, offering generous grounds and a superb location within walking distance of Letterkenny town centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.0 x 4.0\nLaminated timber flooring. L Shaped hallway with glass panel door on entrance.\n\nLiving Room - 5.3 x 4.5\nLaminated timber flooring. Open fireplace with wooden surround and tiled inset. Bay window promoting natural light. Coving and ceiling rose.\n\nKitchen/Dining Area - 6.6 x 4.5\nTiled flooring in kitchen area. Eye and low level units with double drainer sink. Breakfast bar devides kitchen from dining area. Laminate timber flooring in dining area. Patio door leading to side of property.\n\nUtility Room - 3.0 x 2.0\nTiled flooring. Plumbed for washing machine and tumble dryer. Hot press located here. Door to rear of property.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.7 x 3.5\nLaminated timber flooring. Independent access dorr to rear of property.\n\nGuest WC - 2.2 x 1.3\nLaminated timber flooring. Comprising w.c and wash hand basin.\n\nLanding - 3.7 x 2.1\nCarpet covering on floor. Window promoting natural light on stair return.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.5 x 3.5\nCarpet covering on floor. Velux & dormer windows promoting natural light. Built in wardrobe.\n\nEnsuite - 2.0 x 1.0\nLaminated timber flooring and partially tiled walls. Comprising w.c, wash hand basin and electric shower.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.3 x 3.3\nCarpet covering on floor.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nThree piece suite comprising w.c, wash hand basin and electric shower.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Detached Family Home</li><li>Located in the popular residential area of College Farm Road.</li><li>Convenient to town centre and all its amenities</li><li>Constructed 1995</li><li>Total floor area 135 sq m</li><li>Comprising 3 bedrooms, 1 of which is on ground floor</li><li>Main bedroom on first floor is ensuite.</li><li>Presented well throughout</li><li>Occupying 0.4 acre site</li><li>Garden to front and rear of property</li><li>Tarmac Driveway and stone patio area to rear.</li><li>Garden shed included in sale</li><li>Services include: Oil fired heating, Public water and Septic tank for sewage disposal</ul>"
